model {

  dispatcher = dispatcher "bo loop — the dispatcher" {
    description '''
**What it is:** `CLI/beads-loop.sh` — the one command (`bo loop`) that turns beads tickets into background workers.

Steps it runs, one per tick:
1. reads the branches already at work (`branchesCurrentlyAtWork`)
2. claims a ticket atomically with `bd ready --claim`
3. matches its single dispatching label against the `AGENT` map — never guesses a specialist
4. reads `branch` and `parent` off the claim; never invents a branch
5. walks the parent chain to the epic gate and publishes its branch + PR if missing (`ensureEpicGatePr`)
6. makes sure the branch's worktree exists (`ensureWorktree`)
7. spawns `claude --bg --agent <agent> --permission-mode bypassPermissions` with cwd inside that worktree
8. logs one line and moves on — it never polls a worker, never reaps, never merges
'''
  }

  hook = hook "hooks/worker-stop.sh — the Stop hook" {
    description '''
**What it is:** the fail-closed gatekeeper that fires when a worker session stops.

Steps:
1. checks `$BO_DONE_FILE` — no marker, no commit, no push, no PR, no close (`ERROR reason=not-declared-done`)
2. commits the work onto the ticket's `branch` and pushes it
3. opens the PR once per branch (base = the epic gate's `branch`, `main` at the epic tier) or reuses it
4. writes the PR url onto the ticket as `metadata.pr`

It closes a *task* only on its done marker. A worker that touches the marker before the brief is complete has filed half a task onto a shared branch — the one failure this model cannot undo on its own.
'''
  }

  beads = beadsStore "beads DB (bd)" {
    description '''
**What it is:** the beads issue database — the loop's only runtime input. None of the contract docs are read at runtime; the graph lives here.

Verbs the tower uses: `bd ready --claim` (atomic — a bare `bd ready` would let two loops steal the same ticket), `bd unclaim`, `bd heartbeat`, `bd create -t gate -l <label> --parent <id>`, `bd dep add <a> <b> --type blocks`, `bd update --set-metadata` (merges — it never disturbs the plan's `branch`), `bd show --json`.
'''
  }

  origin = remote "origin — GitHub" {
    description '''
**What it is:** the remote the tower publishes to. `main` at the bottom, one PR per branch above it: `feature/<slug>` → PR → the epic branch, `epic/<slug>` → PR → `main`.
'''
  }

  human = human "Human (Brodie)" {
    description '''
**What it is:** the only one who closes gates. Workers leave their tickets open and report in their final message; the human reads the report, verifies the branch, and closes. A claimable ticket assigned to a human is a model bug — the person enters through gates and closes them; nothing is spawned for them.
'''
  }

  decisions = noteDoc "Decision points" {
    description '''
**What it is:** the judgments the machine cannot make — everything else is mechanical.

- **Plan-epic:** what the epic *is* — one epic, one `epic/<slug>` of 2–4 lowercase words saying what the thing is.
- **Plan-feature:** what counts as a complete user-facing flow; phasing foundations → core → dependent → polish; a colliding sibling gets **different words**, never `-2`.
- **Order inside a feature's line:** logic, then its tests, then the UI — never a fan.
- **Tier of a test ticket:** the label carries the tier, not `--agent`; a mis-labeled ticket gets the wrong depth of coverage and no worker can tell you it did.
- **Gates:** the human verifies feature-review / epic-review output, then closes. Nothing self-closes.
- **Merge conflicts at the epic tier:** the `merge` agent resolves between feature branches; it writes no code and never merges into `main`.
'''
  }

  workers = layer "The workers (the spokes)" {
    engineer = worker "engineer" {
      style { icon bootstrap:code-slash }
      description '''
**What it is:** the back-end worker — business logic, endpoints, hooks, types, error factories. Spawned `s b w`, certified by respawn. Never writes tests, JSX, or CSS. Dispatched by the label `backend-logic`.
'''
    }
    testerUnit = worker "tester-unit" {
      style { icon tech:flask }
      description '''
**What it is:** the **micro tier** — one back-end function alone; every branch, boundary, empty/null, error. Never a component (the UI is proved by the composition tier). Label `unit-tests`, framework skill `framework-jest`.
'''
    }
    frontend = worker "frontend" {
      style { icon bootstrap:browser-chrome }
      description '''
**What it is:** the UI worker — components, layout, styling, the shared component system. Built last, against functions already proved. Label `frontend-ui`.
'''
    }
    testerFeature = worker "tester-feature" {
      style { icon tech:flask }
      description '''
**What it is:** the **composition tier** — one feature's pieces proved wired; its errors and successes surface. Never re-runs the unit tier's edge-case matrix. Label `feature-test`, skill `framework-playwright`.
'''
    }
    testerE2e = worker "tester-e2e" {
      style { icon tech:flask }
      description '''
**What it is:** the **broad tier** — journeys across features on the real stack; cross-feature state; one success + one failure per feature. Label `epic-e2e-test`, skill `framework-playwright`.
'''
    }
    reviewAgent = worker "review" {
      style { icon bootstrap:shield-check }
      description '''
**What it is:** the reviewer — three questions from first principles: does the code do what its source of truth demands, do the tests prove it, is it simple and readable. Maps the system (entry → exit, following imports), instruments it with trace logs, runs the tests against the instrumented code, posts findings as PR comments. Files no tickets; commits and pushes nothing. Labels `feature-review` and `epic-review`.
'''
    }
    mergeAgent = worker "merge" {
      style { icon bootstrap:arrows-collapse }
      description '''
**What it is:** the epic-tier assembler — reads the feature branches off the feature gates, assembles them onto the epic branch in its own worktree, resolves the conflicts between them, runs the tests, reports. Writes no code, no tests; never merges into `main`, never opens a PR. Label `epic-merge-pr`.
'''
    }
  }

  planAgents = layer "The plan agents (outside the tower)" {
    planEpic = planner "plan-epic" {
      description '''
**What it is:** conversational epic architect — vague idea → clarifying questions → research → exactly one epic gate plus `epic-merge-pr`, `epic-e2e-test`, `epic-review`. Writes the gate's own `branch` (`epic/recipe-box`) onto the gate and its three tickets as their **only** metadata key.
'''
    }
    planFeature = planner "plan-feature" {
      description '''
**What it is:** breaks an epic into feature-sized features — complete user-facing flows — each with its own `feature/<slug>` branch, its `feature-test` and `feature-review` tickets, phased by dependency. `parent-child` to the epic. Never writes a `pr`, never writes a PR base.
'''
    }
    planTask = planner "plan-task" {
      description '''
**What it is:** breaks ONE feature into tasks, each `parent-child` to the feature, **labeled at creation** with `bd create -l <label>`, the feature's `branch` copied **verbatim** (a plan agent never invents a branch below its own tier), chained onto their predecessor, every ticket verified with a `bd show --json` round trip.
'''
    }
  }

  errors = layer "The alarm vocabulary" {
    labelAmbiguous = failure "ERROR reason=label-ambiguous" {
      #error #leftClaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** zero or two dispatching labels on a claim. The dispatcher never guesses a specialist — the ticket is LEFT CLAIMED so its lease parks it off the frontier, and the errors file is the alarm.
'''
    }
    metadataMissing = failure "ERROR reason=metadata-missing" {
      #error #leftClaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** no `branch` in the claim's metadata — a plan agent skipped its one key. Left claimed, same treatment as a mislabelled ticket. The loop never invents a branch.
'''
    }
    branchBusy = failure "ERROR reason=branch_busy held=N" {
      #error #unclaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** tickets exist and are claimable, but every branch they want is already working. The freshly claimed ticket goes straight back (`bd unclaim`) and the tick tries the next one — up to `max_parallel + 2` claims per tick. One pair of hands per branch.
'''
    }
    worktreeFailed = failure "ERROR reason=worktree-failed" {
      #error #leftClaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** `git worktree add` failed under `.claude/worktrees/`. Left claimed — a worker spawned in a missing folder burns a slot on nothing.
'''
    }
    workerNotDispatched = failure "ERROR reason=worker-not-dispatched" {
      #error #unclaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** `claude --bg` spawned no session. The ticket is put back with `bd unclaim` so the next tick can retry it.
'''
    }
    epicPrFailed = failure "ERROR reason=epic-pr-failed step=…" {
      #error #leftClaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** the epic branch or its PR could not be published. Steps: `walk`, `gate-branch`, `forge`, `missing-tool`, `push`, `pr`, `annotate`. Left claimed — a worker spawned under an epic branch that does not exist burns a slot and files a commit nobody can pull.
'''
    }
    notDeclaredDone = failure "ERROR reason=not-declared-done" {
      #error #leftClaimed
      description '''
**What it is:** the Stop hook fired but `$BO_DONE_FILE` was never touched. Fail-closed: no commit, no push, no PR, no close. The ticket stays claimed so its lease parks it off the frontier and every task chained behind it waits.
'''
    }
    noPrTarget = failure "ERROR reason=no-pr-target" {
      #error
      description '''
**What it is:** the Stop hook found no PR target the loop never handed down — named for the target, since `pr` now means the url.
'''
    }
    frontierEmpty = failure "reason=frontier_empty" {
      #stateProbe
      description '''
**What it is:** the empty frontier's first state — nothing left to do.
'''
    }
    towerStalled = failure "reason=tower_stalled waiting=N" {
      #stateProbe
      description '''
**What it is:** the empty frontier's second state — work exists but sits off the frontier behind an open blocker, an open gate most often, which only a human can clear. `tick()` probes the difference with `bd list --status open,blocked --limit 0`.
'''
    }
    maxParallelStalled = failure "max_parallel_stalled" {
      #stateProbe
      description '''
**What it is:** at capacity (counted fresh each tick from `claude agents --json`) with nothing `in_progress`.
'''
    }
  }

  tower = layer "The tower (one beads DB)" {
    epic = gate "Epic — Recipe Box (RECIPE-1)" {
      description '''
**What it is:** the epic gate — the "what"; the human closes it once, after `epic-review` is done.

- **Branch:** `epic/recipe-box` → PR → `main` (the loop publishes it and writes `pr` as its metadata)
- **Waits on:** `RECIPE-4` epic-review — the gate-waits-on-its-child edge lives in bd, invisible to this map
- **Nothing but the loop ever publishes this branch.** Every feature PR below it targets it.
'''
      epicMergePr = ticket "epic-merge-pr (RECIPE-2)" {
        description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    assemble the feature branches onto epic/recipe-box
label:    epic-merge-pr        agent: merge
metadata: { "branch": "epic/recipe-box" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-5, RECIPE-11 (the feature gates)
```
**Brief:** read the feature branches off the feature gates, assemble them onto the epic branch in your own worktree, resolve the conflicts between them, run the tests, report. No code, no tests, no merge into main, no PR.
'''
      }
      epicE2e = ticket "epic-e2e-test (RECIPE-3)" {
        description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    journeys across the whole app in a real browser
label:    epic-e2e-test        agent: tester-e2e (respawn)
metadata: { "branch": "epic/recipe-box" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-2
```
**Brief:** cross-feature state handoffs, session continuity, one success + one failure journey per feature. Never re-test the unit tier's edges or the feature tier's wiring.
'''
      }
      epicReview = ticket "epic-review (RECIPE-4)" {
        description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    the three questions over the whole epic
label:    epic-review          agent: review (respawn)
metadata: { "branch": "epic/recipe-box" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-3
```
**Brief:** map entry → exit, instrument with trace logs, run the tests against the instrumented code, post findings as PR comments. Then the human verifies and closes the epic gate.
'''
      }
      featA = gate "Feature — Add a Recipe (RECIPE-5)" {
        description '''
**What it is:** the feature gate for one complete user-facing flow: a user writes a recipe and sees it in the box. Human closes it once `feature-review` is done.

- **Branch:** `feature/add-recipe` → PR → `epic/recipe-box` (base read off the epic gate, never copied down)
- **Waits on:** `RECIPE-10` feature-review (edge lives in bd; a gate never blocks its own children — they are claimable while it is open)
- The loop wrote `pr` onto the ticket that first landed work here.
'''
        backendA = ticket "backend-logic (RECIPE-6)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    validateRecipe + saveRecipe — pure functions
label:    backend-logic        agent: engineer
category: backend-logic
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" }   ← copied verbatim from the feature gate
depends:  none (first task — it is the frontier)
```
**Requirements**
1. `validateRecipe(input): Either<RecipeValidationError, Recipe>` — pure, no mutation
2. `saveRecipe(validated): RecipeRecord` through the repository port only
3. reject: empty title, title > 120 chars, duplicate slug, missing ingredients

**Files:** `src/recipes/validate-recipe.ts`, `src/recipes/types.ts`, `src/recipes/ports.ts`
**Done:** report in the final message; the Stop hook, not you, files it.
'''
        }
        unitA = ticket "unit-tests (RECIPE-7)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    exhaustive coverage for validateRecipe
label:    unit-tests           agent: tester-unit (respawn)
category: unit-tests
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-6 (the back-end ticket it tests)
skill:    framework-jest
```
**Cover:** every branch, every boundary (120/121 chars), empty/null input, each error it throws, empty ingredients list.
**Owned elsewhere:** composition wiring (feature tier), components (never here), journeys (epic tier).
'''
        }
        frontendA = ticket "frontend-ui (RECIPE-8)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    RecipeForm + RecipeCard against proved functions
label:    frontend-ui          agent: frontend
category: frontend-ux
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-7
```
**Brief:** the form, validation feedback surfacing each RecipeValidationError, the card in the box. Layout and styling only — the logic is already proved by the micro tier.
'''
        }
        featureTestA = ticket "feature-test (RECIPE-9)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    the add-recipe pieces are wired
label:    feature-test         agent: tester-feature (respawn)
category: feature-test
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-8 (the LAST task — nothing is proved against half a feature)
skill:    framework-playwright
```
**Cover:** the composed flow saves a recipe; each encapsulated error surfaces to the user. The suite runs only after every task landed on the feature branch.
'''
        }
        featureReviewA = ticket "feature-review (RECIPE-10)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    the three questions over feature/add-recipe
label:    feature-review       agent: review (respawn)
category: review
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-9 (no review before the suite)
skill:    pr-comments
```
**Brief:** three questions from first principles, findings as PR comments. Then the human verifies and closes gate RECIPE-5.
'''
        }
      }
      featB = gate "Feature — Search the Box (RECIPE-11)" {
        description '''
**What it is:** the feature gate for one complete user-facing flow: a user searches saved recipes by title and ingredient. Human closes it once its review is done.

- **Branch:** `feature/search-recipes` → PR → `epic/recipe-box`
- **Waits on:** `RECIPE-16` feature-review (edge lives in bd)
- Runs **side by side** with Add a Recipe — two features in parallel, each feature alone on its branch.
'''
        backendB = ticket "backend-logic (RECIPE-12)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    searchRecipes — pure filter over the repository port
label:    backend-logic        agent: engineer
category: backend-logic
metadata: { "branch": "feature/search-recipes" }
depends:  none (first task — with Add a Recipe, it is the frontier; claimed together)
```
**Requirements**
1. `searchRecipes(query, records): Recipe[]` — pure, deterministic order
2. empty query returns all, sorted newest first; whitespace trimmed
3. no match returns `[]`, never an error

**Files:** `src/recipes/search-recipes.ts`, `src/recipes/ports.ts` (read side)
'''
        }
        unitB = ticket "unit-tests (RECIPE-13)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    exhaustive coverage for searchRecipes
label:    unit-tests           agent: tester-unit (respawn)
category: unit-tests
metadata: { "branch": "feature/search-recipes" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-12
skill:    framework-jest
```
**Cover:** empty query, whitespace, unicode titles, empty store, tie-break ordering, case folding.
'''
        }
        frontendB = ticket "frontend-ui (RECIPE-14)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    SearchBar + live results list
label:    frontend-ui          agent: frontend
category: frontend-ux
metadata: { "branch": "feature/search-recipes" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-13
```
**Brief:** debounce, empty-state copy, highlight matches with the shared component system.
'''
        }
        featureTestB = ticket "feature-test (RECIPE-15)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    the search pieces are wired
label:    feature-test         agent: tester-feature (respawn)
category: feature-test
metadata: { "branch": "feature/search-recipes" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-14 (the LAST task)
skill:    framework-playwright
```
'''
        }
        featureReviewB = ticket "feature-review (RECIPE-16)" {
          description '''
**What's inside the ticket:**
```
title:    the three questions over feature/search-recipes
label:    feature-review       agent: review (respawn)
category: review
metadata: { "branch": "feature/search-recipes" }
depends:  blocked-by RECIPE-15
skill:    pr-comments
```
'''
        }
      }
    }

    // the chain inside each feature: one linked line, never a fan —
    // logic, then its tests, then the UI; suite after the last task; review after the suite
    featA.backendA -[blocks]-> featA.unitA
    featA.unitA -[blocks]-> featA.frontendA
    featA.frontendA -[blocks]-> featA.featureTestA
    featA.featureTestA -[blocks]-> featA.featureReviewA

    featB.backendB -[blocks]-> featB.unitB
    featB.unitB -[blocks]-> featB.frontendB
    featB.frontendB -[blocks]-> featB.featureTestB
    featB.featureTestB -[blocks]-> featB.featureReviewB

    // epic tier: the merge waits on the feature gates; e2e after merge; review after e2e
    featA -[blocks]-> epic.epicMergePr
    featB -[blocks]-> epic.epicMergePr
    epic.epicMergePr -[blocks]-> epic.epicE2e
    epic.epicE2e -[blocks]-> epic.epicReview
  }

  // the AGENT map: one edge per dispatching label — that label alone decides the worker
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.engineer "backend-logic"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.testerUnit "unit-tests"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.frontend "frontend-ui"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.testerFeature "feature-test"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.testerE2e "epic-e2e-test"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.reviewAgent "feature-review"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.reviewAgent "epic-review"
  dispatcher -[dispatches]-> workers.mergeAgent "epic-merge-pr"

  // each worker points at the tickets its label owns
  workers.engineer -[works]-> tower.featA.backendA
  workers.engineer -[works]-> tower.featB.backendB
  workers.testerUnit -[works]-> tower.featA.unitA
  workers.testerUnit -[works]-> tower.featB.unitB
  workers.frontend -[works]-> tower.featA.frontendA
  workers.frontend -[works]-> tower.featB.frontendB
  workers.testerFeature -[works]-> tower.featA.featureTestA
  workers.testerFeature -[works]-> tower.featB.featureTestB
  workers.testerE2e -[works]-> tower.epicE2e
  workers.reviewAgent -[works]-> tower.featA.featureReviewA
  workers.reviewAgent -[works]-> tower.featB.featureReviewB
  workers.reviewAgent -[works]-> tower.epicReview
  workers.mergeAgent -[works]-> tower.epicMergePr

  // the plan agents build the tower top-down, each writing only its own tier's branch
  planAgents.planEpic -[plans]-> tower.epic "one epic + its three tickets"
  planAgents.planFeature -[plans]-> tower.featA "flow-sized features"
  planAgents.planFeature -[plans]-> tower.featB "flow-sized features"
  planAgents.planTask -[plans]-> tower.featA.backendA "tasks, chained"
  planAgents.planTask -[plans]-> tower.featB.backendB "tasks, chained"

  // only a human closes a gate
  human -[closes]-> tower.epic "after epic-review"
  human -[closes]-> tower.featA "after feature-review"
  human -[closes]-> tower.featB "after feature-review"

  // the lease and the publishing
  workers.engineer -> beads "bd heartbeat — keep the lease alive"
  workers.engineer -> origin "commit on the branch (via the Stop hook, never directly)"
  dispatcher -> beads "bd ready --claim / bd unclaim"
  dispatcher -> origin "ensureEpicGatePr — push epic branch, open PR, write pr on the gate"
  hook -> origin "commit, push, PR — only when BO_DONE_FILE exists"

  // where the errors pop up
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.labelAmbiguous
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.metadataMissing
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.branchBusy
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.worktreeFailed
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.workerNotDispatched
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.epicPrFailed
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.frontierEmpty
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.towerStalled
  dispatcher -[raises]-> errors.maxParallelStalled
  hook -[raises]-> errors.notDeclaredDone
  hook -[raises]-> errors.noPrTarget
}
